course: dictionary
lesson: 11439
title: The addressee
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The addressee is the person a letter, parcel, email or message is sent to. You are the sender, the person who sends it. Look for the addressee on the envelope or in the «To» line of an email.
explain: «Dear Mrs Patel, your parcel is on its way.» Mrs Patel is the addressee, because the letter is written to her. Her name and address go on the envelope, so the post office knows where to take it.
explain: Addressee has a second meaning, about talking. When someone speaks, the addressee is the person they are speaking to. «Sam, can you pass the salt?» Sam is the addressee, because Sam is the one being spoken to.
fact: Addressee is a noun. Its plural is addressees.
fact: The addressee is the person a letter, parcel, email or message is sent to.
fact: The sender is the person who writes or sends the letter, parcel or message.
fact: «Return to sender if addressee unknown» means the post goes back to the sender if the addressee cannot be found.
fact: In speech, the addressee is the person someone is speaking to.
exercise: «Please write the addressee's name on the envelope.» What is the addressee? | The stamp on the envelope | The person who sends the letter | *The person the letter is sent to | The post office worker
exercise: In an email, where do you find the addressee? | *In the «To» line | In the subject line | In the attachment | At the very bottom, after your name
exercise: «Max, look at this!» said Ella. Who is the addressee? | Ella | *Max | The message | The screen
test: Where does the addressee's name and address go on a letter? | Inside the postbox | Under the table | *On the envelope | On the back of the stamp
test: What is the plural of addressee? | addressers | addressies | addressen | *addressees
exam: What does addressee mean when someone is talking? | A loud noise in the room | A kind of envelope | *The person being spoken to | The person who is speaking
